msgid "Dropping the axes does not mean forgiving them. A row is proven only when *every* job it had was green: one red or aborted combination un-proves it, however many green siblings it has. Only a priority row can have several, since it deploys its whole cross-product at once while a regular row gets one combination per sweep -- and letting a green compose job carry a red swarm one would walk the regular line past a combination nobody fixed."
